{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145886",
      "title": "Merging \"head\" Content",
      "lectureOrder": 309,
      "videoOrder": 287,
      "sourceHash": "16327fa3546fdf8b71b1ae6aa8def8543dfc471c4001c694889f36ec7fd7be43",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "Now in the last lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 6.36,
          "en": "we added <Head> to the _appJS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.36,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "There is an important implication of this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 12.297,
          "en": "Now we have to have the <Head> element there in appJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.297,
          "end": 14.3,
          "en": "and we of course still also have it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.3,
          "end": 15.86,
          "en": "in our page components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.86,
          "end": 17.85,
          "en": "In indexJS in the events folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 20.28,
          "en": "for example, I also have <Head>.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 23.6,
          "en": "And as you see on the rendered page, both is applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.6,
          "end": 27.05,
          "en": "The title and description from the page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.05,
          "end": 30.83,
          "en": "and the viewport from the _appJS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.83,
          "end": 32.498,
          "en": "And this is important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.498,
          "end": 37.498,
          "en": "NextJS automatically merges multiple <Head> elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.69,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "So if you set a <Head> here in _appJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 42.34,
          "en": "and then also in the page component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.34,
          "end": 46.47,
          "en": "the content of those different <Head> sections gets merged.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "Even if we would have multiple <Head> sections here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 51.21,
          "en": "inside of a single component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.21,
          "end": 54.45,
          "en": "the content would be merged by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.45,
          "end": 57.92,
          "en": "But of course that means that we could also have conflicts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.92,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "For example, I could have a another <title> set here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 66,
          "en": "for whatever reasons, and now I set a <title> here and here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66,
          "end": 69.69,
          "en": "Now NextJS automatically merges your <Head> sections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.69,
          "end": 73.28,
          "en": "and it also resolves such conflicts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.28,
          "end": 77.83,
          "en": "If I add multiple titles here and I reload this Events page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.83,
          "end": 82.113,
          "en": "you see only one title shows up here, not multiple titles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.12,
          "end": 85.61,
          "en": "It simply takes the latest element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.61,
          "end": 88.85,
          "en": "if you have to same element multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.85,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "So if we have the <title> here and here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 93.1,
          "en": "the second <title> wins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.1,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "The same would be true for meta elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 97.00999999999999,
          "en": "with a name attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.00999999999999,
          "end": 98.93,
          "en": "If you have other <Head> content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.93,
          "end": 100.47999999999999,
          "en": "which is neither a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.47999999999999,
          "end": 103.64,
          "en": "nor a meta element with the name attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.64,
          "end": 107.78,
          "en": "but let's say a meta element with some other attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.78,
          "end": 110.723,
          "en": "then you can always add a manual key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.9,
          "end": 115.34,
          "en": "like description to still allow NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.34,
          "end": 118.6,
          "en": "to find out if two elements are clashing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.6,
          "end": 121.55,
          "en": "And then, again, the latter one will win.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.55,
          "end": 124.77,
          "en": "Now, of course, this is redundant code here, this extra head",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "I just wanted to show this NextJS behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 131.26,
          "en": "And that it does have an important implication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.26,
          "end": 135.28,
          "en": "because it means that in _appJS, we can indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.28,
          "end": 138.03,
          "en": "also go into the head section we set up there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.03,
          "end": 142.11,
          "en": "and define a general title that applies to all pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.11,
          "end": 144.07999999999998,
          "en": "unless it's overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.07999999999998,
          "end": 147.47,
          "en": "This ensures that we always have a title on every page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.47,
          "end": 150.53,
          "en": "even if we forget to set a page specific one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.53,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "which we, of course, typically want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 157.14,
          "en": "So here, I'll then give all my pages a general title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.14,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "and also a general description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 164.73,
          "en": "Again, that will be overwritten by the page specific data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.73,
          "end": 167.55,
          "en": "but in case we don't have page specific data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.55,
          "end": 170.66,
          "en": "then this general data would kick in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.66,
          "end": 173.73,
          "en": "So here I have my general <Head> setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.73,
          "end": 177.09,
          "en": "but if I reload this All Events page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.09,
          "end": 178.78,
          "en": "we don't see that there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.78,
          "end": 181.75,
          "en": "Because we do have page specific data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.75,
          "end": 186.01,
          "en": "and that then overrides the more general data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.01,
          "end": 188.89,
          "en": "Because the page component is rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.89,
          "end": 190.26,
          "en": "after the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.26,
          "end": 192.2,
          "en": "So the later <Head> section wins",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.2,
          "end": 193.68,
          "en": "and that will be the head section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.68,
          "end": 195.253,
          "en": "instead of the page component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
